IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc28-part24-s752`
IMPORT `ccc28-part24a-dangerous-offender`

-- ccc28-tests-part24a.l4 -- tests of sections 752.01 to 753.02. Expected values are written by hand from the words of each provision, on both sides of
-- every threshold (two years less a day and two years, the sixtieth and sixty-first day, the thirtieth and thirty-first, six months and a day after).

§ `Test fixtures (not law)`

`s 752.01 test a designated offence` MEANS
    `s 752 offence` OF `s 752 an offence under this Act as it now reads`, (`Provision of the Code` OF 266, ""), `s 752 convicted of the offence itself`, (Date 1 1 2020), FALSE

`s 752.01 test an offence that is not designated` MEANS
    `s 752 offence` OF `s 752 an offence under this Act as it now reads`, (`Provision of the Code` OF 86, ""), `s 752 convicted of the offence itself`, (Date 1 1 2020), FALSE

`s 752.01 test a primary designated offence` MEANS
    `s 752 offence` OF `s 752 an offence under this Act as it now reads`, (`Provision of the Code` OF 271, ""), `s 752 convicted of the offence itself`, (Date 1 1 2020), FALSE

GIVEN o IS A `s 752 offence`
      t IS A `Length of time`
      against IS A BOOLEAN
      spio IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 752.01 previous conviction`
`s 752.01 test a previous conviction` MEANS `s 752.01 previous conviction` OF o, t, against, spio

GIVEN o IS A `s 752 offence`
      t IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A `s 752.01 previous conviction`
`s 752.01 test a plain previous conviction` MEANS `s 752.01 test a previous conviction` o t FALSE (JUST FALSE)

`s 752.01 test two designated previous convictions with two years` MEANS
    LIST `s 752.01 test a plain previous conviction` `s 752.01 test a designated offence` `two years`
       , `s 752.01 test a plain previous conviction` `s 752.01 test a designated offence` `five years`

§ `s 752.01: the prosecutor advises the court`

#ASSERT `s 752.01 the prosecutor shall advise the court whether the prosecutor intends to make an application under subsection 752.1(1)` TRUE `s 752.01 test a designated offence` FALSE `s 752.01 test two designated previous convictions with two years` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- opinion held; (a): designated offence and two previous convictions of at least two years
#ASSERT `s 752.01 the prosecutor shall advise the court whether the prosecutor intends to make an application under subsection 752.1(1)` FALSE `s 752.01 test a designated offence` FALSE `s 752.01 test two designated previous convictions with two years` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no opinion that the offence is a serious personal injury offence
#ASSERT `s 752.01 the prosecutor shall advise the court whether the prosecutor intends to make an application under subsection 752.1(1)` TRUE `s 752.01 test an offence that is not designated` FALSE `s 752.01 test two designated previous convictions with two years` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (a) needs a designated offence, and (b) needs the offence against an intimate partner or family
#ASSERT `s 752.01 the prosecutor shall advise the court whether the prosecutor intends to make an application under subsection 752.1(1)` TRUE `s 752.01 test a designated offence` FALSE (LIST `s 752.01 test a plain previous conviction` `s 752.01 test a designated offence` `two years`) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- only one previous conviction
#ASSERT `s 752.01 the prosecutor shall advise the court whether the prosecutor intends to make an application under subsection 752.1(1)` TRUE `s 752.01 test a designated offence` FALSE (LIST `s 752.01 test a plain previous conviction` `s 752.01 test a designated offence` `two years`, `s 752.01 test a plain previous conviction` `s 752.01 test a designated offence` `two years less a day`) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the second sentence was two years less a day, below two years
#ASSERT `s 752.01 the prosecutor shall advise the court whether the prosecutor intends to make an application under subsection 752.1(1)` TRUE `s 752.01 test a designated offence` FALSE (LIST `s 752.01 test a plain previous conviction` `s 752.01 test a designated offence` `two years`, `s 752.01 test a plain previous conviction` `s 752.01 test an offence that is not designated` `ten years`) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the second previous conviction was not of a designated offence
#ASSERT `s 752.01 the prosecutor shall advise the court whether the prosecutor intends to make an application under subsection 752.1(1)` TRUE `s 752.01 test an offence that is not designated` TRUE (LIST `s 752.01 test a previous conviction` `s 752.01 test a designated offence` `two years` TRUE (JUST FALSE), `s 752.01 test a previous conviction` `s 752.01 test an offence that is not designated` (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE) TRUE (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b): against an intimate partner or family; a previous designated offence, and a previous serious personal injury offence
#ASSERT `s 752.01 the prosecutor shall advise the court whether the prosecutor intends to make an application under subsection 752.1(1)` TRUE `s 752.01 test an offence that is not designated` FALSE (LIST `s 752.01 test a previous conviction` `s 752.01 test a designated offence` `two years` TRUE (JUST FALSE), `s 752.01 test a previous conviction` `s 752.01 test an offence that is not designated` (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE) TRUE (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b) needs the present offence committed against such a person
#ASSERT `s 752.01 the prosecutor shall advise the court whether the prosecutor intends to make an application under subsection 752.1(1)` TRUE `s 752.01 test an offence that is not designated` TRUE (LIST `s 752.01 test a previous conviction` `s 752.01 test a designated offence` `two years` FALSE (JUST FALSE), `s 752.01 test a previous conviction` `s 752.01 test an offence that is not designated` (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE) TRUE (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b): only one previous conviction was against such a person
#ASSERT `s 752.01 the prosecutor shall advise the court whether the prosecutor intends to make an application under subsection 752.1(1)` TRUE `s 752.01 test an offence that is not designated` TRUE (LIST `s 752.01 test a previous conviction` `s 752.01 test a designated offence` `two years` TRUE (JUST FALSE), `s 752.01 test a previous conviction` `s 752.01 test an offence that is not designated` (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE) TRUE NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING   -- (b): whether the second previous conviction was a serious personal injury offence is not covered, and it might make two
#ASSERT `s 752.01 the prosecutor shall advise the court whether the prosecutor intends to make an application under subsection 752.1(1)` TRUE `s 752.01 test an offence that is not designated` TRUE (LIST `s 752.01 test a previous conviction` `s 752.01 test an offence that is not designated` `two years` TRUE NOTHING, `s 752.01 test a previous conviction` `s 752.01 test an offence that is not designated` (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE) TRUE NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING   -- (b): two previous convictions, each not known to be serious personal injury offences
#ASSERT `s 752.01 the prosecutor shall advise the court whether the prosecutor intends to make an application under subsection 752.1(1)` TRUE `s 752.01 test an offence that is not designated` TRUE (LIST `s 752.01 test a previous conviction` `s 752.01 test an offence that is not designated` `two years` TRUE (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b): one previous conviction, not a designated offence or a serious personal injury offence

-- the same duty as a regulative rule: advise before sentence is imposed (30 days after the finding of guilt is the day sentence is imposed)
#TRACE `s 752.01 the prosecutor's duty to advise the court` 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the prosecutor` DOES `s 752.01 advise the court whether the prosecutor intends to make an application under subsection 752.1(1)` AT 29

#TRACE `s 752.01 the prosecutor's duty to advise the court` 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the prosecutor` DOES `s 752.01 advise the court whether the prosecutor intends to make an application under subsection 752.1(1)` AT 30

#TRACE `s 752.01 the prosecutor's duty to advise the court` 30 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 31)

#ASSERT `s 752.01 the prosecutor advised the court before sentence was imposed` 30 30 EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- on the day sentence is imposed
#ASSERT `s 752.01 the prosecutor advised the court before sentence was imposed` 31 30 EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the day after
#ASSERT `s 752.01 the prosecutor advised the court before sentence was imposed` 0 30 EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `s 752.1: remand for assessment`

#ASSERT `s 752.1(1) the court shall remand the offender for an assessment` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- convicted of a serious personal injury offence
#ASSERT `s 752.1(1) the court shall remand the offender for an assessment` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- convicted of an offence referred to in paragraph 753.1(2)(a)
#ASSERT `s 752.1(1) the court shall remand the offender for an assessment` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no application by the prosecutor
#ASSERT `s 752.1(1) the court shall remand the offender for an assessment` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the court is not of the opinion
#ASSERT `s 752.1(1) the court shall remand the offender for an assessment` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- neither kind of offence
#ASSERT `s 752.1(1) the court shall remand the offender for an assessment` TRUE TRUE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- the answer of s 752 is not covered
#ASSERT `s 752.1(1) the court shall remand the offender for an assessment` TRUE TRUE NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the other kind holds
#ASSERT `s 752.1(1) the remand is for a period not exceeding 60 days` 60 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 752.1(1) the remand is for a period not exceeding 60 days` 61 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#TRACE `s 752.1(1) the court's duty to remand the offender` 20 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 752.1(1) remand the offender by order in writing to the custody of a person designated by the court` AT 20

#TRACE `s 752.1(1) the court's duty to remand the offender` 20 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 21)

#TRACE `s 752.1(2) the duty of the person to whom the offender is remanded` 0 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 752.1(2) the person to whom the offender is remanded` DOES `s 752.1(2) file a report of the assessment with the court` AT 30

#TRACE `s 752.1(2) the duty of the person to whom the offender is remanded` 0 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 31)

#TRACE `s 752.1(2) the duty of the person to whom the offender is remanded` 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 752.1(2) the person to whom the offender is remanded` DOES `s 752.1(2) file a report of the assessment with the court` AT 60

#ASSERT `s 752.1(2) the report is filed not later than 30 days after the end of the assessment period` 30 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 752.1(2) the report is filed not later than 30 days after the end of the assessment period` 31 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 752.1(2) the report is filed not later than 30 days after the end of the assessment period` 60 30 EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the court extended the period by 30 days
#ASSERT `s 752.1(2) the report is filed not later than 30 days after the end of the assessment period` 61 30 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 752.1(2) the last day on which the report is filed in time` (Date 1 3 2021) 0 EQUALS Date 31 3 2021   -- 30 days after 1 March 2021
#ASSERT `s 752.1(2) the last day on which the report is filed in time` (Date 1 3 2021) 30 EQUALS Date 30 4 2021   -- extended by 30 days

#ASSERT `s 752.1(3) the court may extend the period within which the report must be filed` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 752.1(3) the court may extend the period within which the report must be filed` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no application by the prosecutor
#ASSERT `s 752.1(3) the court may extend the period within which the report must be filed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the court is not satisfied: a grant limited by its own wording, not covered
#ASSERT `s 752.1(3) the court may extend the period within which the report must be filed` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 752.1(3) the extension is by a maximum of 30 days` 30 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 752.1(3) the extension is by a maximum of 30 days` 31 EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 753: the finding that an offender is a dangerous offender`

#ASSERT `s 753(1) the court shall find the offender to be a dangerous offender` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a) with the threat and limb (i)
#ASSERT `s 753(1) the court shall find the offender to be a dangerous offender` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a) with the threat and limb (ii)
#ASSERT `s 753(1) the court shall find the offender to be a dangerous offender` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a) with the threat and limb (iii)
#ASSERT `s 753(1) the court shall find the offender to be a dangerous offender` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (a) with the threat but no limb
#ASSERT `s 753(1) the court shall find the offender to be a dangerous offender` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (a) with a limb but no threat
#ASSERT `s 753(1) the court shall find the offender to be a dangerous offender` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b) with the failure to control sexual impulses
#ASSERT `s 753(1) the court shall find the offender to be a dangerous offender` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b) without it
#ASSERT `s 753(1) the court shall find the offender to be a dangerous offender` FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no application after a report
#ASSERT `s 753(1) the court shall find the offender to be a dangerous offender` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the offence is within neither paragraph of the definition
#ASSERT `s 753(1) the court shall find the offender to be a dangerous offender` TRUE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- whether the offence is within (a) is not covered, and (b) does not hold
#ASSERT `s 753(1) the court shall find the offender to be a dangerous offender` TRUE NOTHING (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b) holds though (a) is not covered

#ASSERT `s 753(1.1) the conditions in paragraph (1)(a) or (b) are presumed to have been met` `s 752.01 test a primary designated offence` TRUE (LIST `s 752.01 test a plain previous conviction` `s 752.01 test a primary designated offence` `two years`, `s 752.01 test a plain previous conviction` `s 752.01 test a primary designated offence` `five years`) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 753(1.1) the conditions in paragraph (1)(a) or (b) are presumed to have been met` `s 752.01 test a primary designated offence` TRUE (LIST `s 752.01 test a plain previous conviction` `s 752.01 test a primary designated offence` `two years`, `s 752.01 test a plain previous conviction` `s 752.01 test a primary designated offence` `five years`) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the contrary is proved
#ASSERT `s 753(1.1) the conditions in paragraph (1)(a) or (b) are presumed to have been met` `s 752.01 test a primary designated offence` TRUE (LIST `s 752.01 test a plain previous conviction` `s 752.01 test a primary designated offence` `two years`, `s 752.01 test a plain previous conviction` `s 752.01 test a primary designated offence` `two years less a day`) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the second sentence was two years less a day
#ASSERT `s 753(1.1) the conditions in paragraph (1)(a) or (b) are presumed to have been met` `s 752.01 test a primary designated offence` TRUE (LIST `s 752.01 test a plain previous conviction` `s 752.01 test a primary designated offence` `two years`) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- only one previous conviction
#ASSERT `s 753(1.1) the conditions in paragraph (1)(a) or (b) are presumed to have been met` `s 752.01 test a designated offence` TRUE (LIST `s 752.01 test a plain previous conviction` `s 752.01 test a primary designated offence` `two years`, `s 752.01 test a plain previous conviction` `s 752.01 test a primary designated offence` `five years`) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the present offence is designated but not primary designated
#ASSERT `s 753(1.1) the conditions in paragraph (1)(a) or (b) are presumed to have been met` `s 752.01 test a primary designated offence` FALSE (LIST `s 752.01 test a plain previous conviction` `s 752.01 test a primary designated offence` `two years`, `s 752.01 test a plain previous conviction` `s 752.01 test a primary designated offence` `five years`) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the court is not satisfied that a sentence of two years or more would be appropriate

#ASSERT `s 753(2) the application is made not later than six months after the imposition of sentence` (Date 15 3 2021) (Date 15 9 2021) EQUALS TRUE   -- the last day
#ASSERT `s 753(2) the application is made not later than six months after the imposition of sentence` (Date 15 3 2021) (Date 16 9 2021) EQUALS FALSE   -- a day after
#ASSERT `s 753(2) the application is made not later than six months after the imposition of sentence` (Date 31 8 2021) (Date 28 2 2022) EQUALS TRUE   -- six months after 31 August is the last day of February
#ASSERT `s 753(2) the application is made not later than six months after the imposition of sentence` (Date 31 8 2021) (Date 1 3 2022) EQUALS FALSE   -- the day after
#ASSERT `s 753(2)(a) the notice was given and the application is not later than six months after the imposition of sentence` TRUE (Date 15 3 2021) (Date 15 9 2021) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 753(2)(a) the notice was given and the application is not later than six months after the imposition of sentence` FALSE (Date 15 3 2021) (Date 15 9 2021) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no notice before sentence
#ASSERT `s 753(2)(a) the notice was given and the application is not later than six months after the imposition of sentence` TRUE (Date 15 3 2021) (Date 16 9 2021) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- more than six months
#ASSERT `s 753(2)(b) relevant evidence became available in the interim and the application is not later than six months after the imposition of sentence` TRUE (Date 15 3 2021) (Date 15 9 2021) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 753(2)(b) relevant evidence became available in the interim and the application is not later than six months after the imposition of sentence` FALSE (Date 15 3 2021) (Date 15 9 2021) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no new evidence
#ASSERT `s 753(2)(b) relevant evidence became available in the interim and the application is not later than six months after the imposition of sentence` TRUE (Date 15 3 2021) (Date 16 9 2021) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- more than six months
#ASSERT `s 753(2)(a) and (b) apply` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 753(2)(a) and (b) apply` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 753(2)(a) and (b) apply` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 753(2) the application under subsection (1) is made in time` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- before sentence, whatever paragraphs (a) and (b) say
#ASSERT `s 753(2) the application under subsection (1) is made in time` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- after sentence, paragraphs (a) and (b) apply
#ASSERT `s 753(2) the application under subsection (1) is made in time` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- after sentence, they do not
#ASSERT `s 753(2) the application under subsection (1) is made in time` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- after sentence, whether they apply is not covered
#ASSERT `s 753(3) an application under subsection 752.1(1) may be made after the imposition of sentence or after the offender begins to serve the sentence` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 753(3) an application under subsection 752.1(1) may be made after the imposition of sentence or after the offender begins to serve the sentence` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 753(3) an application under subsection 752.1(1) may be made after the imposition of sentence or after the offender begins to serve the sentence` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 753(4) the disposition is within paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` TRUE `s 753(4)(a) a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 753(4) the disposition is within paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` TRUE (`s 753(4)(b) a sentence for the offence with an order for long-term supervision` `two years` `ten years`) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the minimum term and the longest supervision period
#ASSERT `s 753(4) the disposition is within paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` TRUE (`s 753(4)(b) a sentence for the offence with an order for long-term supervision` `two years less a day` `ten years`) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- below the minimum punishment of two years
#ASSERT `s 753(4) the disposition is within paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` TRUE (`s 753(4)(b) a sentence for the offence with an order for long-term supervision` `two years` (`Length of time` OF 10, 0, 1, FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a supervision period of ten years and a day
#ASSERT `s 753(4) the disposition is within paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` TRUE `s 753(4)(c) a sentence for the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 753(4) the disposition is within paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` TRUE `s 753(4) a disposition the subsection does not name` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 753(4) the disposition is within paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` FALSE `s 753(4)(a) a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the court did not find a dangerous offender

#ASSERT `s 753(4.1) the court shall impose a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- no reasonable expectation that a lesser measure will protect the public
#ASSERT `s 753(4.1) the court shall impose a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the court is satisfied that a lesser measure will protect the public
#ASSERT `s 753(4.1) the court shall impose a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a dangerous offender: the subsection is silent

#ASSERT `s 753(4.2) the sentence imposed replaces the sentence that was imposed for the offence` TRUE (JUST TRUE) `s 753(4)(a) a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 753(4.2) the sentence imposed replaces the sentence that was imposed for the offence` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (`s 753(4)(b) a sentence for the offence with an order for long-term supervision` `two years` `ten years`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 753(4.2) the sentence imposed replaces the sentence that was imposed for the offence` TRUE (JUST TRUE) `s 753(4)(c) a sentence for the offence` EQUALS NOTHING   -- the subsection names (4)(a) and (4)(b) only
#ASSERT `s 753(4.2) the sentence imposed replaces the sentence that was imposed for the offence` FALSE (JUST TRUE) `s 753(4)(a) a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the application was not made after the offender began to serve the sentence
#ASSERT `s 753(4.2) the sentence imposed replaces the sentence that was imposed for the offence` TRUE (JUST FALSE) `s 753(4)(a) a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not a case to which (2)(a) and (b) apply
#ASSERT `s 753(4.2) the sentence imposed replaces the sentence that was imposed for the offence` TRUE NOTHING `s 753(4)(a) a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 753(5) the court may take this course` TRUE `s 753(5)(a) treat the application as an application to find the offender to be a long-term offender` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 753(5) the court may take this course` TRUE `s 753(5)(a) find that the offender is a long-term offender` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 753(5) the court may take this course` TRUE `s 753(5)(a) hold another hearing for that purpose` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 753(5) the court may take this course` TRUE `s 753(5)(b) impose sentence for the offence for which the offender has been convicted` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 753(5) the court may take this course` TRUE `s 753(5) a course the subsection does not name` EQUALS NOTHING   -- list not closed
#ASSERT `s 753(5) the court may take this course` FALSE `s 753(5)(b) impose sentence for the offence for which the offender has been convicted` EQUALS NOTHING   -- the court found a dangerous offender: the subsection's "if" gate is not met, and the text does not say the court may not

§ `s 753.01: later conviction of a dangerous offender`

#ASSERT `s 753.01(1) the court shall remand the offender for an assessment` TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- later convicted of a serious personal injury offence
#ASSERT `s 753.01(1) the court shall remand the offender for an assessment` TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- later convicted of an offence under subsection 753.3(1)
#ASSERT `s 753.01(1) the court shall remand the offender for an assessment` FALSE (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not found to be a dangerous offender
#ASSERT `s 753.01(1) the court shall remand the offender for an assessment` TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no application by the prosecutor
#ASSERT `s 753.01(1) the court shall remand the offender for an assessment` TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- neither kind of offence
#ASSERT `s 753.01(1) the court shall remand the offender for an assessment` TRUE NOTHING FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the answer of s 752 is not covered
#ASSERT `s 753.01(1) the remand is for a period not exceeding 60 days` 60 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 753.01(1) the remand is for a period not exceeding 60 days` 61 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#TRACE `s 753.01(2) the duty of the person to whom the offender is remanded` 0 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 752.1(2) the person to whom the offender is remanded` DOES `s 753.01(2) file a report of the assessment with the court` AT 30

#TRACE `s 753.01(2) the duty of the person to whom the offender is remanded` 0 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 31)

#ASSERT `s 753.01(2) the report is filed not later than 30 days after the end of the assessment period` 30 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 753.01(2) the report is filed not later than 30 days after the end of the assessment period` 31 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 753.01(2) the report is filed not later than 30 days after the end of the assessment period` 60 30 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 753.01(3) the court may extend the period within which the report must be filed` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 753.01(3) the court may extend the period within which the report must be filed` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 753.01(3) the court may extend the period within which the report must be filed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 753.01(3) the court may extend the period within which the report must be filed` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- both gates fail: the "On application" gate is tested first and answers JUST FALSE (fork F16.3; the other reading for the if gate is F3.3)
#ASSERT `s 753.01(3) the extension is by a maximum of 30 days` 30 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 753.01(3) the extension is by a maximum of 30 days` 31 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 753.01(4) the prosecutor may apply for this sentence or order` TRUE `s 753.01(4) an application for a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 753.01(4) the prosecutor may apply for this sentence or order` TRUE `s 753.01(4) an application for an order that the offender be subject to a new period of long-term supervision` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 753.01(4) the prosecutor may apply for this sentence or order` TRUE `s 753.01(4) an application the subsection does not name` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 753.01(4) the prosecutor may apply for this sentence or order` FALSE `s 753.01(4) an application for a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- before the report is filed
#ASSERT `s 753.01(5) the court shall impose a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 753.01(5) the court shall impose a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the court is satisfied that a sentence will protect the public
#ASSERT `s 753.01(5) the court shall impose a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the application is not for that sentence
#ASSERT `s 753.01(6) the court shall order that the offender be subject to a new period of long-term supervision` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 753.01(6) the court shall order that the offender be subject to a new period of long-term supervision` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the court is satisfied that the sentence alone will protect the public
#ASSERT `s 753.01(6) the court shall order that the offender be subject to a new period of long-term supervision` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the application is not for a new period

§ `s 753.02: a victim's evidence`

#ASSERT `s 753.02 the evidence is deemed also to have been given during the hearing` TRUE `s 753.02 a hearing under paragraph 753(5)(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 753.02 the evidence is deemed also to have been given during the hearing` TRUE `s 753.02 a hearing under subsection 753.01(5)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 753.02 the evidence is deemed also to have been given during the hearing` TRUE `s 753.02 a hearing under subsection 753.01(6)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 753.02 the evidence is deemed also to have been given during the hearing` TRUE `s 753.02 a hearing the section does not name` EQUALS NOTHING   -- limited by its own wording
#ASSERT `s 753.02 the evidence is deemed also to have been given during the hearing` FALSE `s 753.02 a hearing under paragraph 753(5)(a)` EQUALS NOTHING   -- evidence not given by a victim on a subsection 753(1) application: not covered
